[0.6766579999999998,"o","Schema and role findings\r\n"]
[0.7299219999999993,"o","  [HIGH] Broad default table privilege\r\n"]
[0.7821869999999995,"o","    Scope: rls_doctor_demo\r\n"]
[0.8346579999999992,"o","    Defaults for owner postgres in schema rls_doctor_demo grant grantee authenticated privilege INSERT; Application role authenticated. Future tables created by postgres can receive this object privilege without an explicit table grant; actual access also requires schema USAGE.\r\n"]
[0.8866889999999996,"o","    Fix: Revoke the broad default privilege and grant only the table privileges required by each application role.\r\n"]
[0.939012,"o","\r\n"]
[0.9912419999999997,"o","rls_doctor_demo.orders\r\n"]
[1.044352,"o","  RLS disabled; force RLS disabled; 0 policies\r\n"]
[1.0967919999999998,"o","  [HIGH] RLS-disabled table is reachable by an application role\r\n"]
[1.1495479999999993,"o","    rls_doctor_demo.orders has no row-level checks; Application role authenticated and can exercise INSERT granted to authenticated.\r\n"]
[1.2042189999999993,"o","    Fix: Enable RLS and add least-privilege policies for each application role.\r\n"]
[1.2565539999999995,"o","    Suggested SQL:\r\n"]
[1.309291,"o","      alter table \"rls_doctor_demo\".\"orders\" enable row level security;\r\n"]
[1.3615489999999992,"o","      -- Then add policies that match your access model before exposing this table to client roles.\r\n"]
[1.4137709999999997,"o","\r\n"]
[1.4671999999999992,"o","rls_doctor_demo.profiles\r\n"]
[1.5195239999999997,"o","  RLS enabled; force RLS disabled; 2 policies\r\n"]
[1.572006,"o","  [HIGH] TRUNCATE is reachable by an application role\r\n"]
[1.6242509999999992,"o","    rls_doctor_demo.profiles can be truncated; Application role authenticated and can exercise TRUNCATE granted to authenticated. RLS never protects TRUNCATE.\r\n"]
[1.6765169999999996,"o","    Fix: Revoke TRUNCATE from application-facing roles and grant it only to isolated maintenance roles.\r\n"]
[1.7314509999999999,"o","  [INFO] FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY is disabled\r\n"]
[1.7846349999999997,"o","    The table owner bypasses RLS while FORCE RLS is disabled. Superusers and BYPASSRLS roles bypass RLS regardless of FORCE RLS.\r\n"]
[1.8371559999999993,"o","    Fix: Enable FORCE RLS for sensitive multi-tenant tables after confirming owner-side maintenance workflows.\r\n"]
[1.8916789999999999,"o","    Suggested SQL:\r\n"]
[1.9440979999999994,"o","      alter table \"rls_doctor_demo\".\"profiles\" force row level security;\r\n"]
[1.9967029999999992,"o","  [CRITICAL] Anonymous-style role can write rows too broadly\r\n"]
[2.0488609999999996,"o","    Policy \"anon can update profiles\" allows UPDATE for public with an unconditional predicate.\r\n"]
[2.1012389999999996,"o","    Fix: Require authenticated ownership constraints in USING and WITH CHECK for writes.\r\n"]
[2.1533559999999996,"o","    Suggested SQL:\r\n"]
[2.2060829999999996,"o","      -- Adapt this suggested SQL to your schema and access model before executing it.\r\n"]
[2.258044999999999,"o","      alter policy \"anon can update profiles\"\r\n"]
[2.3100120000000004,"o","        on \"rls_doctor_demo\".\"profiles\"\r\n"]
[2.362836999999999,"o","        to authenticated\r\n"]
[2.4148879999999995,"o","        using ((select auth.uid()) = <owner_column>)\r\n"]
[2.4670369999999995,"o","        with check ((select auth.uid()) = <owner_column>);\r\n"]
[2.5193659999999998,"o","  [MEDIUM] Write policy has no explicit WITH CHECK expression\r\n"]
[2.573848,"o","    Policy \"anon can update profiles\" handles UPDATE without an explicit insert/update constraint.\r\n"]
[2.62598,"o","    Fix: Add WITH CHECK so new or changed rows must satisfy the same ownership and tenant boundaries.\r\n"]
[2.677852999999999,"o","    Suggested SQL:\r\n"]
[2.731380999999999,"o","      -- Adapt this suggested SQL to your schema and access model before executing it.\r\n"]
[2.7834649999999996,"o","      alter policy \"anon can update profiles\"\r\n"]
[2.834702,"o","        on \"rls_doctor_demo\".\"profiles\"\r\n"]
[2.888150999999999,"o","        with check ((select auth.uid()) = <owner_column>);\r\n"]
[2.9412710000000004,"o","  [LOW] Public-like role uses a permissive policy\r\n"]
[2.994382,"o","    Policy \"anon can update profiles\" is permissive, so it is OR-combined with other permissive policies.\r\n"]
[3.047922,"o","    Fix: Review whether the policy should be restrictive or scoped to authenticated application roles.\r\n"]
[3.099658,"o","  [HIGH] Anonymous-style role can read rows unconditionally\r\n"]
[3.151323999999999,"o","    Policy \"anyone can read profiles\" grants SELECT to public with no row predicate.\r\n"]
[3.2030589999999997,"o","    Fix: Restrict the policy with tenant, owner, or explicit public-content predicates.\r\n"]
[3.254987,"o","    Suggested SQL:\r\n"]
[3.3061819999999997,"o","      -- Adapt this suggested SQL to your schema and access model before executing it.\r\n"]
[3.3580559999999995,"o","      alter policy \"anyone can read profiles\"\r\n"]
[3.4106430000000003,"o","        on \"rls_doctor_demo\".\"profiles\"\r\n"]
[3.4618319999999994,"o","        using (<public_read_predicate>);\r\n"]
[3.512988,"o","  [LOW] Public-like role uses a permissive policy\r\n"]
[3.5642639999999997,"o","    Policy \"anyone can read profiles\" is permissive, so it is OR-combined with other permissive policies.\r\n"]
[3.6154010000000003,"o","    Fix: Review whether the policy should be restrictive or scoped to authenticated application roles.\r\n"]
